ladder = '''    static List<String> neighbors(String word,Set<String> dictionary){List<String> out=new ArrayList<>();char[] a=word.toCharArray();for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){char old=a[i];for(char c='a';c<='z';c++)if(c!=old){a[i]=c;String next=new String(a);if(dictionary.contains(next))out.add(next);}a[i]=old;}return out;}
    static Map<String,Integer> wordDistances(String begin,Set<String> words){Map<String,Integer> d=new HashMap<>();Queue<String> q=new ArrayDeque<>();q.offer(begin);d.put(begin,0);while(!q.isEmpty()){String w=q.poll();for(String next:neighbors(w,words))if(!d.containsKey(next)){d.put(next,d.get(w)+1);q.offer(next);}}return d;}'''
gadd('Word ladder I',ladder+'''\n    public static int solve(String begin,String end,String[] dictionary){if(begin.equals(end))return 1;Set<String> words=new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(dictionary));if(!words.contains(end))return 0;Integer distance=wordDistances(begin,words).get(end);return distance==null?0:distance+1;}''','System.out.println(solve("hit","cog",new String[]{"hot","dot","dog","lot","log","cog"}));','5',
    'One lowercase letter changes per step, every intermediate/end word in dictionary; return shortest sequence length in WORDS, zero absent.', 'Implicit unit-edge word graph; BFS discovers shortest change count. Add one to count the starting word.', 'O(W*L²*26) time under Java string creation/hash costs; O(W*L) strings/space.',edges='All words must have equal length and lowercase a..z. begin=end returns one even if not in dictionary.')
gadd('Word ladder II',ladder+'''\n    static void paths(String current,String begin,Set<String> words,Map<String,Integer> d,List<String> reversed,List<List<String>> out){reversed.add(current);if(current.equals(begin)){List<String> path=new ArrayList<>(reversed);Collections.reverse(path);out.add(path);}else for(String before:neighbors(current,words))if(d.containsKey(before)&&d.get(before)==d.get(current)-1)paths(before,begin,words,d,reversed,out);reversed.remove(reversed.size()-1);}
    public static List<List<String>> solve(String begin,String end,String[] dictionary){Set<String> words=new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(dictionary));List<List<String>> out=new ArrayList<>();if(!begin.equals(end)&&!words.contains(end))return out;Map<String,Integer> d=wordDistances(begin,words);if(!d.containsKey(end))return out;words.add(begin);paths(end,begin,words,d,new ArrayList<>(),out);out.sort((a,b)->a.toString().compareTo(b.toString()));return out;}''','System.out.println(solve("hit","cog",new String[]{"hot","dot","dog","lot","log","cog"}));','[[hit, hot, dot, dog, cog], [hit, hot, lot, log, cog]]',
    'Return ALL shortest lowercase word transformation sequences.', 'BFS computes shortest distance for each word. Backtrack from end only through neighbors one distance lower; these edges form an acyclic shortest-path graph, enumerating every shortest sequence.', 'BFS O(W*L²*26), plus output-sensitive backtracking; output may be exponential.',edges='Marking one predecessor per word loses alternate shortest sequences; distance-decreasing backtracking preserves all.')
dsu='''    static class DSU {final int[] parent,size;DSU(int n){parent=new int[n];size=new int[n];for(int i=0;i<n;i++){parent[i]=i;size[i]=1;}}int find(int x){while(x!=parent[x]){parent[x]=parent[parent[x]];x=parent[x];}return x;}boolean union(int a,int b){a=find(a);b=find(b);if(a==b)return false;if(size[a]<size[b]){int t=a;a=b;b=t;}parent[b]=a;size[a]+=size[b];return true;} }'''
theory('MST theory', 'A spanning tree connects all V vertices using V-1 edges and no cycle. An MST minimizes total weight. If the graph is disconnected there is no spanning tree; algorithms may instead return a minimum spanning forest. Cut property: a minimum-weight edge across any cut can be included in an MST, because exchanging it for the edge an MST uses across that cut cannot increase weight. Kruskal sorts edges and accepts ones connecting separate components (DSU). Prim repeatedly adds the smallest edge connecting the built tree to an outside vertex. Negative edge weights are fine for MST. Directed graphs require different arborescence algorithms.')
gadd('Disjoint Set',dsu,'DSU d=new DSU(4); d.union(0,1); d.union(1,2); System.out.println(d.find(0)==d.find(2)); System.out.println(d.find(0)==d.find(3));','true\nfalse',
    'Maintain connectivity under union operations; no deletions.', 'Represent each set as a rooted parent tree. Path halving shortens find paths; union-by-size attaches the smaller root beneath the larger.', 'O(alpha(n)) amortized per operation; O(n) storage.',edges='Only representative roots have meaningful aggregate size. Never treat two raw parent entries as final representatives without find.')
gadd('Find the MST weight',dsu+'''\n    public static long solve(int n,int[][] input){if(n==0)return 0;int[][] edges=input.clone();Arrays.sort(edges,(a,b)->Integer.compare(a[2],b[2]));DSU d=new DSU(n);long sum=0;int used=0;for(int[] e:edges)if(d.union(e[0],e[1])){sum+=e[2];used++;}if(used!=n-1)throw new IllegalArgumentException("disconnected graph has no MST");return sum;}''','System.out.println(solve(3,new int[][]{{0,1,5},{1,2,2},{0,2,1}}));','3',
    'Undirected edges [u,v,weight], negative weights allowed; return MST weight or throw if disconnected.', 'Kruskal accepts sorted edges only across different components. Each is a safe cut edge; rejecting same-component edges prevents cycles.', 'O(E log E+E alpha(V)) time; O(V+E) space.',edges='A disconnected graph gives a forest, which this MST API explicitly rejects. Use long total.')
gadd('Number of operations to make network connected',dsu+'''\n    public static int solve(int n,int[][] edges){if(n<=1)return 0;if(edges.length<n-1)return -1;DSU d=new DSU(n);int components=n;for(int[] e:edges)if(d.union(e[0],e[1]))components--;return components-1;}''','System.out.println(solve(4,new int[][]{{0,1},{0,2},{1,2}}));','1',
    'One operation relocates one existing cable; return minimum operations to connect all vertices or -1.', 'Any connected graph needs at least n-1 edges. With enough total edges, redundant cycle edges can connect separate components, needing components-1 relocations.', 'O(V+E alpha(V)) time; O(V) space.')
gadd('Accounts merge',dsu+'''\n    public static List<List<String>> solve(List<List<String>> accounts){DSU d=new DSU(accounts.size());Map<String,Integer> owner=new HashMap<>();for(int i=0;i<accounts.size();i++)for(int j=1;j<accounts.get(i).size();j++){String email=accounts.get(i).get(j);Integer old=owner.putIfAbsent(email,i);if(old!=null)d.union(i,old);}Map<Integer,TreeSet<String>> groups=new TreeMap<>();for(Map.Entry<String,Integer> e:owner.entrySet())groups.computeIfAbsent(d.find(e.getValue()),k->new TreeSet<>()).add(e.getKey());List<List<String>> out=new ArrayList<>();for(Map.Entry<Integer,TreeSet<String>> e:groups.entrySet()){List<String> row=new ArrayList<>();row.add(accounts.get(e.getKey()).get(0));row.addAll(e.getValue());out.add(row);}for(int i=0;i<accounts.size();i++)if(accounts.get(i).size()==1)out.add(new ArrayList<>(accounts.get(i)));return out;}''','System.out.println(solve(Arrays.asList(Arrays.asList("John","a@mail","b@mail"),Arrays.asList("John","b@mail","c@mail"))));','[[John, a@mail, b@mail, c@mail]]',
    'Each account is [name,emails...]. Shared emails imply same person transitively; output merged groups with sorted unique emails.', 'Map each email to its first owner and union later owners. Group email keys by final representative, then sort within each group.', 'O(totalEmails*alpha(accounts)+totalEmails log totalEmails) time; O(accounts+emails) space.',edges='Same-name alone does not imply same person. Accounts sharing an email are assumed to have consistent names; name-only accounts are preserved separately.')
gadd('Number of islands II',dsu+'''\n    public static List<Integer> solve(int rows,int cols,int[][] operations){DSU d=new DSU(rows*cols);boolean[] land=new boolean[rows*cols];int count=0;List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();int[] dr={1,-1,0,0},dc={0,0,1,-1};for(int[] p:operations){int id=p[0]*cols+p[1];if(!land[id]){land[id]=true;count++;for(int k=0;k<4;k++){int r=p[0]+dr[k],c=p[1]+dc[k];if(r>=0&&c>=0&&r<rows&&c<cols&&land[r*cols+c]&&d.union(id,r*cols+c))count--;}}out.add(count);}return out;}''','System.out.println(solve(2,2,new int[][]{{0,0},{1,1},{0,1},{0,0}}));','[1, 2, 1, 1]',
    'Start all water; each operation adds land at a valid cell, returning four-connected island count after every operation.', 'New land adds one component; each successful union with a distinct neighbor component removes one. Repeated land additions change nothing.', 'O(R*C+operations*alpha(R*C)) time; O(R*C) space.',edges='Grid dimensions/product and all coordinates must fit valid int array bounds. Count only successful unions, not every neighboring land cell.')
gadd('Making a large island',dsu+'''\n    public static int solve(int[][] a){if(a.length==0||a[0].length==0)return 0;int m=a.length,n=a[0].length;DSU d=new DSU(m*n);for(int r=0;r<m;r++)for(int c=0;c<n;c++)if(a[r][c]==1){if(r+1<m&&a[r+1][c]==1)d.union(r*n+c,(r+1)*n+c);if(c+1<n&&a[r][c+1]==1)d.union(r*n+c,r*n+c+1);}int best=0;int[] dr={1,-1,0,0},dc={0,0,1,-1};for(int r=0;r<m;r++)for(int c=0;c<n;c++){if(a[r][c]==1){best=Math.max(best,d.size[d.find(r*n+c)]);continue;}Set<Integer> roots=new HashSet<>();for(int k=0;k<4;k++){int x=r+dr[k],y=c+dc[k];if(x>=0&&y>=0&&x<m&&y<n&&a[x][y]==1)roots.add(d.find(x*n+y));}int size=1;for(int root:roots)size+=d.size[root];best=Math.max(best,size);}return best;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{1,0},{0,1}}));','3',
    'Flip at most one zero to one; maximize four-connected island CELLS in a rectangular binary grid.', 'Union existing land, then each possible zero flip joins its DISTINCT adjacent component roots plus one cell. Also retain existing maximum for all-land input.', 'O(R*C*alpha(R*C)) time; O(R*C) space.',edges='Two neighboring cells from the same component must not be counted twice; use a root set. All-water returns one; all-land returns its area.')
gadd('Most stones removed with same row or column',dsu+'''\n    public static int solve(int[][] stones){DSU d=new DSU(stones.length);Map<Integer,Integer> row=new HashMap<>(),col=new HashMap<>();int components=stones.length;for(int i=0;i<stones.length;i++){Integer a=row.putIfAbsent(stones[i][0],i),b=col.putIfAbsent(stones[i][1],i);if(a!=null&&d.union(i,a))components--;if(b!=null&&d.union(i,b))components--;}return stones.length-components;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{0,0},{0,1},{1,0},{1,2},{2,1},{2,2}}));','5',
    'Remove a stone only while another shares its row or column; maximize removals. Coordinates are unique pairs.', 'Union stone indices via a representative for each row and column. Each connected component can remove all but one using a spanning-tree leaf order; at least one must remain.', 'Expected O(N alpha(N)) time; O(N) space.',edges='Rows and columns have separate maps, so identical numeric row/column values are not accidentally identified.')
gadd('Kosaraju\'s algorithm',graph_common+'''\n    static void finish(List<List<Integer>> g,int u,boolean[] seen,List<Integer> out){seen[u]=true;for(int v:g.get(u))if(!seen[v])finish(g,v,seen,out);out.add(u);}
    public static int solve(int n,int[][] edges){List<List<Integer>> g=graph(n,edges,true),rev=graph(n,new int[0][],true);for(int[] e:edges)rev.get(e[1]).add(e[0]);boolean[] seen=new boolean[n];List<Integer> order=new ArrayList<>();for(int u=0;u<n;u++)if(!seen[u])finish(g,u,seen,order);Arrays.fill(seen,false);Collections.reverse(order);int count=0;for(int u:order)if(!seen[u]){count++;visit(rev,u,seen);}return count;}''','System.out.println(solve(4,new int[][]{{0,1},{1,2},{2,0},{2,3}}));','2',
    'Count strongly connected components in a directed graph.', 'DFS finish order ranks SCCs in the condensation DAG. Reverse edges and traverse in decreasing finish time so each DFS remains within one SCC before moving to another.',edges='An SCC requires mutual reachability; weak undirected components solve a different problem.')
lowlink='''    static class Analysis {int time;final int[] in,low;final boolean[] cut;final List<List<int[]>> g=new ArrayList<>();final List<List<Integer>> bridges=new ArrayList<>();Analysis(int n,int[][] edges){in=new int[n];low=new int[n];cut=new boolean[n];Arrays.fill(in,-1);for(int i=0;i<n;i++)g.add(new ArrayList<>());for(int id=0;id<edges.length;id++){int[] e=edges[id];g.get(e[0]).add(new int[]{e[1],id});g.get(e[1]).add(new int[]{e[0],id});}for(int u=0;u<n;u++)if(in[u]<0)dfs(u,-1);}void dfs(int u,int parentEdge){in[u]=low[u]=time++;int children=0;for(int[] e:g.get(u)){int v=e[0];if(e[1]==parentEdge)continue;if(in[v]>=0)low[u]=Math.min(low[u],in[v]);else{children++;dfs(v,e[1]);low[u]=Math.min(low[u],low[v]);if(low[v]>in[u])bridges.add(Arrays.asList(Math.min(u,v),Math.max(u,v)));if(parentEdge!=-1&&low[v]>=in[u])cut[u]=true;}}if(parentEdge==-1&&children>1)cut[u]=true;} }'''
gadd('Bridges in graph',lowlink+'''\n    public static List<List<Integer>> solve(int n,int[][] edges){List<List<Integer>> out=new Analysis(n,edges).bridges;out.sort((a,b)->a.get(0).equals(b.get(0))?Integer.compare(a.get(1),b.get(1)):Integer.compare(a.get(0),b.get(0)));return out;}''','System.out.println(solve(4,new int[][]{{0,1},{1,2},{2,0},{2,3}}));','[[2, 3]]',
    'Return undirected edges whose removal increases component count, endpoint pairs sorted.', 'DFS discovery in[u] and low[u] summarize earliest ancestor reachable from a subtree via at most one back edge. A child edge is a bridge iff low[child]>in[parent].',edges='Track parent EDGE ID, not just parent vertex, so parallel edges correctly provide a back edge and are not falsely reported as bridges.')
gadd('Articulation point in graph',lowlink+'''\n    public static List<Integer> solve(int n,int[][] edges){Analysis a=new Analysis(n,edges);List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();for(int u=0;u<n;u++)if(a.cut[u])out.add(u);return out;}''','System.out.println(solve(4,new int[][]{{0,1},{1,2},{2,0},{2,3}}));','[2]',
    'Return sorted vertices whose removal increases the number of undirected components.', 'A nonroot is a cut vertex if some child subtree has low>=in[root], so it cannot escape above that vertex. A DFS root needs more than one independent DFS child.',edges='Use >= for articulation, > for bridge. The DFS root has a separate condition. Restart DFS for each component.')
